    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Analyze customer feedback with AI and auto-escalate the risky ones\n\nEvery piece of feedback gets read, scored and filed, and the ones that signal a customer about to leave are escalated on their own. Built for founders, support leads and product teams who collect feedback faster than they can read it.\n\n### How it works\n1. A form collects the customer feedback and a code step cleans the text.\n2. Claude returns structured fields: sentiment, theme, severity, churn risk and a short summary.\n3. A guardrail coerces the output to allowed values, then a deterministic rule in code decides escalation: churn risk flagged, or negative sentiment combined with high severity. The decision never depends on the model's mood.\n4. Risky feedback is written to an escalations tab, everything else to a feedback log tab.\n5. Each branch ends with its own confirmation screen, so the person who submitted knows what happened.\n\n### Setup\n1. Add an Anthropic credential on the Chat model node, or swap in any chat model n8n supports.\n2. Add a Google Sheets credential on both Save nodes.\n3. Set the environment variable FEEDBACK_SHEET_ID to a spreadsheet that contains two tabs, named escalations and feedback_log.\n4. Open the form trigger and copy its URL, then share it with customers or paste feedback yourself.\n\n### Customization tips\nThe escalation rule is plain code inside the Guardrail node, so you can tighten or loosen it without prompt engineering. Add your own themes to the attributes in Analyze (AI) to match your product areas.",
        "width": 620,
        "height": 780
      },
